/*!
\page page_stfttpoint StFttPoint

\brief Reconstructed space point in the FTT from combined cluster projections.

\section fttpoint_overview Overview

StFttPoint is a reconstructed space point in the **Forward sTGC Tracker (FTT)**.
It is formed by combining up to four cluster projections (horizontal, vertical, and diagonal
orientations) within a single FTT plane and quadrant.  Both local strip-unit coordinates
and global STAR Cartesian coordinates are stored.

**Detector**: Forward sTGC Tracker (FTT)  
**Stage**: Cluster combination → 2D/3D space point + global coordinate assignment

\section fttpoint_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StFttPoint
\endcode

Stored in \c StFttCollection via \c StPtrVecFttPoint.

\section fttpoint_coordinates Local vs. Global Coordinates

| Set | Access | Units | Description |
|-----|--------|-------|-------------|
| Local | \c x(), \c y() | strip units | Internal reconstruction coordinates |
| Global | \c xyz() | cm | Global STAR Cartesian position |

\section fttpoint_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c UChar_t | \c mPlane | Detector plane (0–3) |
| \c UChar_t | \c mQuadrant | Quadrant A–D (0–3) |
| \c Float_t | \c mX, \c mY | Local strip-unit coordinates |
| \c StFttCluster*[4] | \c mClusters | Parent clusters by readout direction (0–3) |
| \c StThreeVectorD | \c mXYZ | Global STAR position (cm) |
| \c UShort_t | \c mIdTruth, \c mQaTruth | MC truth ID and quality |

\section fttpoint_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c plane(), \c quadrant() | Detector location |
| \c x(), \c y() | Local strip-unit coordinates |
| \c xyz() | Global STAR position (cm) |
| \c nClusters() | Number of contributing cluster projections |
| \c cluster(i) | Parent cluster for direction i |
| \c addCluster(cluster, dir) | Add parent cluster for direction \c dir |
| \c setXYZ(p3) | Set global position |

\section fttpoint_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
for (const StFttPoint* pt : fttColl->points()) {
    const StThreeVectorD& xyz = pt->xyz(); // global cm
    double gx = xyz.x();
    double gy = xyz.y();
    double gz = xyz.z();
    size_t nCl = pt->nClusters();
}
\endcode

\see StFttCluster, StFttRawHit, StFttCollection
*/
